this label */ } ctf_lblent_t; Each label has two different compo‐
nents, a name and a type identifier.  The name is encoded in  the
member  which  is in the format defined in the section Generally,
the names of all labels are found in the internal string section.
The type identifier encoded in the member refers to the last type
identifier that a label refers to in the  current  file.   Labels
only  refer to types in the current file, if the file is a child,
then it will have the same label as its parent; however, its  la‐
bel  will  only  refer to its types, not its parents.  It is also
possible, though rather uncommon, for a file to have multiple la‐
bels.  Labels are placed one after another,  every  eight  bytes.
